Libraries should give callers an error they can match on. Define an **enum** with one variant per downstream error, then implement three things:

1. `std::fmt::Display`, so it can be printed;
2. `std::error::Error`, so it fits wherever errors are expected (`source()` can return the wrapped error);
3. `From<DownstreamError>` for each variant, so `?` converts automatically.

